WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:01.410
Good morning Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:05.130
As you can tell from the gray speckled walls
behind me, I am in an airport, and as you

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:08.860
can tell from my cold dead eyes, it's 5:42
in the morning.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.059
Also, I forgot my camcorder, so I'm filming
this on my phone.

00:00:12.059 --> 00:00:15.090
I have a bunch of things to tell you, but
I also wanna give you some travel tips, so

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:16.500
I'm gonna intersperse them.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.990
Thing One Hank, The Paper Towns Movie: they
moved the release date; it is now coming out

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.699
on July 24th.

00:00:21.699 --> 00:00:24.490
That is the real date; it will really come
out on that day, I think.

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.550
That's very good news, because it means that
Jake and everybody will have time to actually

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:28.550
finish the movie.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:30.119
Also, there is going to be a trailer soon.

00:00:30.119 --> 00:00:31.119
How soon?

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:32.590
I can't tell you, but pretty soon.

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:37.500
Ok, travel tip: In almost every airport in
the United States, there is a gate that is

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.330
empty all the time.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.510
In our case in Indianapolis, it's gate A3.

00:00:41.510 --> 00:00:45.129
This is where I come to make videoblogs, because
there are no people here.

00:00:45.129 --> 00:00:49.440
If you're at an airport, take the time to
walk around and find the empty gate, because

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:52.390
there are plugs, and chairs, and freedom.

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:56.310
Sadly that travel tip does not apply to people
in Los Angeles, New York, Chicago, or Atlanta.

00:00:56.310 --> 00:00:59.940
Thing Two, The Looking For Alaska movie: So
Hank, my first book, Looking For Alaska, came

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:03.629
out 10 years ago, and the movie rights have
been owned ever since by Paramount.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:07.750
But suddenly, it seems like a Looking For
Alaska movie might actually happen, because

00:01:07.750 --> 00:01:09.140
the team has gotten back together.

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:13.210
The same screenwriters who wrote The Fault
In Our Stars and Paper Towns, Scott Neustadter

00:01:13.210 --> 00:01:15.159
and Mike Weber are gonna be writing the script.

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:19.130
And the producers of both Fault In Our Stars
and Paper Towns have joined in as well, so

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:20.800
that is very exciting.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.460
Travel Tip: So, this is the fancy airport
lounge.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:25.869
Don't pay to go to the airport lounge, it's
never worth it.

00:01:25.869 --> 00:01:28.230
You think there's gonna be like milk and honey
and beds in there.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:29.230
You know what they have?

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:30.350
I'll tell you exactly what's in there.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.380
Alcohol and cookies.

00:01:32.380 --> 00:01:34.270
That's it, that's what you will find in the
airport lounge.

00:01:34.270 --> 00:01:38.880
So unless you really love to drink, or are
Cookie Monster, there is no way that it's

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:39.880
worth it.

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:42.680
If you want to go to a quiet, private place
in the airport, don't go to the lounge, go

00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:43.930
to the chapel.

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:47.729
Almost every airport has a chapel, and they
are always nice, and pleasant, and very quiet

00:01:47.729 --> 00:01:48.729
places.

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:51.719
Hank, I noticed most of my travel tips are
like "How do you get away from other travelers?"

00:01:51.719 --> 00:01:55.920
Hank, the biggest movie news of all is that
I have seen the Paper Towns movie, and it

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:56.950
is great.

00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:59.980
I'm just so psyched about it and so grateful
to everyone who's working on it.

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:04.479
Hank, it's one thing to be faithful to a book's
plot; it's another to be faithful to the themes

00:02:04.479 --> 00:02:05.479
of a book.

00:02:05.479 --> 00:02:08.970
And I really feel like the Paper Towns movie
is about learning to imagine others complexly,

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:10.530
I'm just so psyched about it.

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.410
No spoilers, but I am psyched!

00:02:12.410 --> 00:02:16.170
Final travel tip, Hank: When walking on the
moving walkway, be very careful not to step

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.750
on a crack, lest you break your mother's back.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:19.880
Ok Hank, I have to go board.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:21.250
Sorry about the iPhone video.

00:02:21.250 --> 00:02:22.970
July 24th - Paper Towns movie!

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:24.210
I'll see you on Friday!

